> Explain the difference between RAM and storage in three sentences.
RAM is a type of volatile memory that temporarily holds data and programs for quick access during computer operation. Storage is a non-volatile medium that permanently retains data even when the computer is turned off. RAM is used for active tasks, while storage is used for long-term data retention.

